{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"tail -f|Monitoring progress|heartbeat|parent-death|--heartbeat|Dispatch result status|completed|timed_out|failed\" tools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md tools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md'","aggregated_output":"error: Can't create the symlink for multishells at \"/run/user/1001/fnm_multishells/8_1782865751757\". Maybe there are some issues with permissions for the directory? Read-only file system (os error 30)\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:3:A process supervisor for Codex CLI subprocesses. Sits between the orchestrator and a Codex worker, handling process group isolation, two-phase timeout, heartbeat events, and structured result reporting.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:9:Without the dispatcher, the orchestrator calls `codex exec` directly as a raw subprocess. If Codex hangs (stdin stall, long reasoning silence, subprocess wedge), the orchestrator waits forever. There are no heartbeats, no timeout, no structured results -- just a log file and hope.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:15:- **Emits heartbeat events** every 15 seconds so the orchestrator can distinguish \"thinking\" from \"dead\"\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:33:  │ emits heartbeats to stderr every 15s\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:92:The dispatch result is a single JSON object on stdout. In `--json` mode stdout carries **only** that one object; all events, heartbeats, and diagnostics go to stderr. Do not merge the two streams (`2>&1`) when parsing the result -- the concatenated event lines will make `jq` or `serde_json` fail. Redirect stderr elsewhere (e.g. `2>>dispatch.log`), as the examples above do.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:96:  \"status\": \"completed\",\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:119:### Monitoring progress\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:125:{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":15,\"last_activity\":\"running: cargo test\"}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:128:{\"type\":\"heartbeat\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"elapsed_s\":30,\"last_activity\":\"writing: src/lib.rs\"}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:130:{\"type\":\"dispatch_end\",\"dispatch_id\":\"...\",\"ts\":\"...\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"duration_ms\":53311}\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:137:tail -f dispatch.log\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:148:| `--heartbeat` | `15` | Seconds between heartbeat events emitted to stderr |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:167:If the worker exits cleanly after SIGTERM (during the grace period), the dispatch result reports `timed_out` with the worker's final output preserved.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:184:| 0 | Dispatch completed successfully |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:185:| 1 | Dispatch failed or timed out |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:188:## Dispatch result status\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:192:| `completed` | Worker exited 0 and output file exists (if `--output` was specified) |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:193:| `timed_out` | Two-phase timeout fired. `error.retryable` is true. |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/README.md:194:| `failed` | Worker exited non-zero, output file missing, or spawn error |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:3:Rust process supervisor for Codex CLI subprocesses. Spawns `codex exec` with process group isolation, two-phase timeout, NDJSON heartbeat events, and structured JSON results.\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:12:                  timeout select loop, heartbeat, result finalization\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:14:                  parent-death detection (kqueue on macOS, prctl on Linux)\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:17:  event.rs        NDJSON event emitter, heartbeat ticker, stream mode filtering\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:21:  engine.rs       Timeout and heartbeat tests with mock child processes\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:44:- **Output**: Stdout for machine-readable data (DispatchResult JSON), stderr for diagnostics (heartbeats, events, warnings).\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:46:- **Exit codes**: 0 = success (completed), 1 = dispatch failure (failed, timed_out), 2 = CLI error (bad args, missing binary).\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:58:| engine | `internal/engine/loop.go:167-981` | Dispatch function, two-phase timeout, heartbeat |\ntools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md:60:| engine | `internal/event/event.go` | Event emitter, heartbeat ticker |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
